# What is written beside the two packages rather than being a part of either: the state of an editor, the output of a
# build, and the scratch the two were worked out in. None of it is published, and none of it is read by anything.

# The state of an editor or of an IDE, which is whoever is reading the tree rather than the tree.
.idea
.vs
# What Godot imports: a cache of a project, written beside it rather than being a part of it.
.godot/

# What a build writes.
[Dd]ebug
[Rr]elease
[Rr]eleases
[Bb]in
[Oo]bj
[Ll]og